Rem ==================================================================
Rem seedsinq.shoddy — reckoner seed: querying a list
Rem
Rem SORTBY, SORTBYDESC, GROUPBY, MINBY, MAXBY, FINDFIRST, TAKEWHILE and
Rem SKIPWHILE take a LIST and a PROGRAM; DISTINCT, UNION, INTERSECT,
Rem EXCEPT and CHUNK take lists alone.
Rem
Rem     { 3 1 2 } [ ] SORTBY            -> { 1 2 3 }
Rem     { 1 2 3 4 } [ 2 MOD ] GROUPBY   -> { ( 1 . { 1 3 } ) ( 0 . { 2 4 } ) }
Rem
Rem THE PROGRAM ARGUMENT IS THE WHOLE POINT, and it is why eight of the
Rem thirteen words here are RckPureOver rather than RckPure. A program
Rem cannot be run without the dictionary, the registers and the modes it
Rem was typed against, and RckPureOver is the reach reckoner.shoddy opens
Rem to a seed for exactly that. CALL in seedbuiltin.shoddy is the model
Rem followed here; seedeng's ENGDERIV and friends are the same shape.
Rem
Rem Two rules the language sets and this seed inherits: the program sees
Rem the CALLER'S WHOLE SESSION — it may name a word defined a line
Rem earlier and may RCL a register — and whatever it changes is
Rem DISCARDED, because it runs in a sub-evaluation whose state does not
Rem thread home.
Rem
Rem KEYS ARE COMPUTED BEFORE ANYTHING IS ORDERED. Every one of the
Rem selector words runs the program over the whole list first and
Rem refuses on the first failure, in seedeng's pre-flight pattern. A key
Rem program that fails halfway would otherwise leave a half-ordered
Rem answer that looks fine.
Rem
Rem A KEY MUST BE A NUMBER, A STRING OR A FLAG. The first two are what
Rem the < underneath Compare accepts; a flag is admitted because the
Rem predicate words are typed as comparisons and a comparison answers
Rem True or False. Anything else is refused BY NAME rather than silently
Rem mis-sorted, on SORTL's precedent in seedseq.shoddy.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "cuttle.shoddy"
Include "reckoner.shoddy"
Include "sinq.shoddy"
Include "seq.shoddy"

Rem ---- reading a key off a cell -------------------------------------------

Rem A FLAG counts as a key, and has to. TAKEWHILE, SKIPWHILE and
Rem FINDFIRST are predicate words, and a predicate typed at this prompt
Rem ends in a comparison — [ 5 > ] answers True or False, not 1 or 0.
Rem Refusing a flag here would have made three of the thirteen words
Rem unusable with the very programs they are for. False sorts before
Rem True, which is the order 0 before 1 would have given anyway.
Def SnqbSortable(word As String, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case c
        Case CutNum(x)
            Ok(x)
        Case CutStr(s)
            Ok(s)
        Case CutBool(b)
            Ok(Ifte(b, 1, 0))
        Case Else
            Err(RckKindWhy(word, "a NUMBER, a STRING or a TRUE/FALSE key", c), 0)

Rem The decorated element. Three fields and not two, because the key is
Rem needed in BOTH forms: SnqbKey is the bare Number or String, which is
Rem what Compare can order, and SnqbCell is that same key still wrapped
Rem as a cell, which is what GROUPBY has to hand back to the stack.
Rem Shoddy has no runtime type test, so a bare key cannot be re-wrapped
Rem later — it has to be kept.
Rem
Rem Decorating like this also means the program runs ONCE PER ELEMENT
Rem rather than once per comparison, which for a sort is the difference
Rem between n and n log n evaluations of whatever was typed.
Type SnqbHit
    SnqbKey  As t
    SnqbCell As Cell
    SnqbVal  As Cell

Def SnqbKeyPair(word As String, ks As List Of SnqbHit, kc As Cell, x As Cell) As Result
    Select Case SnqbSortable(word, kc)
        Case Ok(k)
            Ok(Prepend(SnqbHit(k, kc, x), ks))
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def SnqbKeyNext(word As String, st As RckState, ts As List Of String, ks As List Of SnqbHit, x As Cell) As Result
    Select Case RckProgOn(word, st, ts, x)
        Case Ok(kc)
            SnqbKeyPair(word, ks, kc, x)
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def SnqbKeyAdd(word As String, st As RckState, ts As List Of String, acc As Result, x As Cell) As Result
    Select Case acc
        Case Ok(ks)
            SnqbKeyNext(word, st, ts, ks, x)
        Case Err(w, at)
            acc
        Case Else
            acc

Rem Every key, or the first reason there is not one. Reverse puts them
Rem back in source order, which is what the stable sort then relies on.
Def SnqbKeys(word As String, st As RckState, ts As List Of String, xs As List Of Cell) As Result
    SnqbKeysDone(Fold(xs, Ok({ }), Fn(acc, x) => SnqbKeyAdd(word, st, ts, acc, x)))

Def SnqbKeysDone(r As Result) As Result
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(ks)
            Ok(Reverse(ks))
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            r

Rem ---- the shape every selector word shares --------------------------------
Rem list on the bottom, program on top, keys computed, then the answer.

Def SnqbOver(word As String, st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell, done As [ List Of SnqbHit -- RckWork ]) As RckWork
    Select Case RckListArg(word, Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(xs)
            SnqbOverProg(word, st, xs, Nth(vs, 2), done)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Def SnqbOverProg(word As String, st As RckState, xs As List Of Cell, pc As Cell, done As [ List Of SnqbHit -- RckWork ]) As RckWork
    Select Case RckProgArg(word, pc)
        Case Ok(ts)
            SnqbOverKeys(word, st, ts, xs, done)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Def SnqbOverKeys(word As String, st As RckState, ts As List Of String, xs As List Of Cell, done As [ List Of SnqbHit -- RckWork ]) As RckWork
    Select Case SnqbKeys(word, st, ts, xs)
        Case Ok(ks)
            Call(done, ks)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Rem ---- SORTBY and SORTBYDESC ------------------------------------------------

Def SnqbSorted(ks As List Of SnqbHit) As RckWork
    RckVals({ CutList(Map(OrderBy(ks, SnqbKey), SnqbVal)) })

Def SnqbSortedDesc(ks As List Of SnqbHit) As RckWork
    RckVals({ CutList(Map(OrderByDesc(ks, SnqbKey), SnqbVal)) })

Def SnqbSeedSort(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RckReg(st, "SORTBY", 2, RckPureOver(Fn(sst, vs) => SnqbOver("SORTBY", sst, vs, SnqbSorted)), "( list prog -- list )", "The list ordered by what the program answers for each element. Equal keys keep the order they were in, so ordering twice orders by both.")
    RckReg(s1, "SORTBYDESC", 2, RckPureOver(Fn(sst, vs) => SnqbOver("SORTBYDESC", sst, vs, SnqbSortedDesc)), "( list prog -- list )", "The same, largest first. Equal keys still keep the order they were in.")

Rem ---- GROUPBY ----------------------------------------------------------------
Rem A group is a PAIR cell of key and member list, so the answer is a
Rem reckoner dictionary and DICTGET reads it without learning anything.

Rem The key cell comes off the group's FIRST member — the earliest
Rem element with that key — and every member carries the same one, so
Rem which is taken does not matter beyond being one that exists.
Def SnqbGroupCell(g As Group) As Cell
    CutPair(Pair(SnqbCell(First(GItems(g))), CutList(Map(GItems(g), SnqbVal))))

Def SnqbGrouped(ks As List Of SnqbHit) As RckWork
    RckVals({ CutList(Map(GroupBy(ks, SnqbKey), SnqbGroupCell)) })

Def SnqbSeedGroup(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "GROUPBY", 2, RckPureOver(Fn(sst, vs) => SnqbOver("GROUPBY", sst, vs, SnqbGrouped)), "( list prog -- list )", "The list gathered into groups by what the program answers, each group a PAIR of the key and its members. Groups come out in the order their keys were first seen, members in the order they were in.")

Rem ---- MINBY, MAXBY, FINDFIRST --------------------------------------------------

Def SnqbLeast(ks As List Of SnqbHit) As RckWork
    Select Case MinByOpt(ks, SnqbKey)
        Case Some(h)
            RckVals({ SnqbVal(h) })
        Case None
            RckWorkBad("MINBY needs a list with something in it")

Def SnqbMost(ks As List Of SnqbHit) As RckWork
    Select Case MaxByOpt(ks, SnqbKey)
        Case Some(h)
            RckVals({ SnqbVal(h) })
        Case None
            RckWorkBad("MAXBY needs a list with something in it")

Rem A key of 0 is the reckoner's false, matching HOW the rest of the
Rem dictionary reads a flag; anything else counts as a hit.
Def SnqbFound(ks As List Of SnqbHit) As RckWork
    Select Case FindOpt(ks, Fn(h) => SnqbKey(h) <> 0)
        Case Some(h)
            RckVals({ SnqbVal(h) })
        Case None
            RckWorkBad("FINDFIRST found nothing the program answered nonzero for")

Def SnqbSeedPick(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RckReg(st, "MINBY", 2, RckPureOver(Fn(sst, vs) => SnqbOver("MINBY", sst, vs, SnqbLeast)), "( list prog -- x )", "The element whose key is smallest. A tie answers the earliest one. Refuses an empty list rather than inventing an answer.")
    Let s2 = RckReg(s1, "MAXBY", 2, RckPureOver(Fn(sst, vs) => SnqbOver("MAXBY", sst, vs, SnqbMost)), "( list prog -- x )", "The element whose key is largest, ties to the earliest.")
    RckReg(s2, "FINDFIRST", 2, RckPureOver(Fn(sst, vs) => SnqbOver("FINDFIRST", sst, vs, SnqbFound)), "( list prog -- x )", "The first element the program answers nonzero for. Refuses when nothing matches, so a miss cannot be mistaken for a value.")

Rem ---- TAKEWHILE and SKIPWHILE -------------------------------------------------

Def SnqbTaken(ks As List Of SnqbHit) As RckWork
    RckVals({ CutList(Map(TakeWhile(ks, Fn(h) => SnqbKey(h) <> 0), SnqbVal)) })

Def SnqbSkipped(ks As List Of SnqbHit) As RckWork
    RckVals({ CutList(Map(SkipWhile(ks, Fn(h) => SnqbKey(h) <> 0), SnqbVal)) })

Def SnqbSeedSlice(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RckReg(st, "TAKEWHILE", 2, RckPureOver(Fn(sst, vs) => SnqbOver("TAKEWHILE", sst, vs, SnqbTaken)), "( list prog -- list )", "The run at the front the program answers nonzero for, stopping at the first it does not.")
    RckReg(s1, "SKIPWHILE", 2, RckPureOver(Fn(sst, vs) => SnqbOver("SKIPWHILE", sst, vs, SnqbSkipped)), "( list prog -- list )", "Everything from the first element the program answers zero for onwards.")

Rem ---- the words that need no program --------------------------------------------
Rem Cells compare structurally, so these mean what they should on
Rem numbers, strings and pairs. A list OF LISTS is the exception: lists
Rem compare by identity, so two separately built ones are never equal.

Def SnqbOneList(word As String, vs As List Of Cell, done As [ List Of Cell -- RckWork ]) As RckWork
    Select Case RckListArg(word, First(vs))
        Case Ok(xs)
            Call(done, xs)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Def SnqbTwoLists(word As String, vs As List Of Cell, done As [ List Of Cell List Of Cell -- RckWork ]) As RckWork
    Select Case RckListArg(word, Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(xs)
            SnqbTwoRight(word, xs, Nth(vs, 2), done)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Def SnqbTwoRight(word As String, xs As List Of Cell, c As Cell, done As [ List Of Cell List Of Cell -- RckWork ]) As RckWork
    Select Case RckListArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(ys)
            Call(done, xs, ys)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Def SnqbDistinct(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    SnqbOneList("DISTINCT", vs, Fn(xs) => RckVals({ CutList(Distinct(xs)) }))

Def SnqbUnion(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    SnqbTwoLists("UNION", vs, Fn(xs, ys) => RckVals({ CutList(Union(xs, ys)) }))

Def SnqbIntersect(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    SnqbTwoLists("INTERSECT", vs, Fn(xs, ys) => RckVals({ CutList(Intersect(xs, ys)) }))

Def SnqbExcept(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    SnqbTwoLists("EXCEPT", vs, Fn(xs, ys) => RckVals({ CutList(Except(xs, ys)) }))

Def SnqbChunkOf(xs As List Of Cell, n As Number) As RckWork
    RckVals({ CutList(Map(Chunk(xs, n), CutList)) })

Def SnqbChunkSize(xs As List Of Cell, c As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckWholeArg("CHUNK", c)
        Case Ok(n)
            SnqbChunkGuard(xs, n)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("CHUNK did not answer")

Rem The guard is here rather than left to the machine because the
Rem machine's Chunk ABORTS on a size below one, and a seed word must
Rem refuse instead: nothing typed at a prompt may end the session.
Def SnqbChunkGuard(xs As List Of Cell, n As Number) As RckWork
    If n < 1 Then
        RckWorkBad("CHUNK needs a batch size of 1 or more")
    Else
        SnqbChunkOf(xs, n)

Def SnqbChunk(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckListArg("CHUNK", Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(xs)
            SnqbChunkSize(xs, Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("CHUNK did not answer")

Def SnqbSeedSets(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RckReg(st, "DISTINCT", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SnqbDistinct(vs)), "( list -- list )", "The list with later repeats dropped, keeping the first sighting of each value in place.")
    Let s2 = RckReg(s1, "UNION", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SnqbUnion(vs)), "( list list -- list )", "Everything in either, each value once, the first list's order first.")
    Let s3 = RckReg(s2, "INTERSECT", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SnqbIntersect(vs)), "( list list -- list )", "Only what is in both, in the first list's order.")
    Let s4 = RckReg(s3, "EXCEPT", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SnqbExcept(vs)), "( list list -- list )", "What is in the first and not the second, in the first list's order.")
    RckReg(s4, "CHUNK", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => SnqbChunk(vs)), "( list n -- list )", "The list cut into batches of n, the last one short if it has to be. Refuses a size below one, which would never finish.")

Rem ---- the seed --------------------------------------------------------------------

Def RckSeedSinq(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = SnqbSeedSort(RckSeeding(st, "seed-sinq"))
    Let s2 = SnqbSeedGroup(s1)
    Let s3 = SnqbSeedPick(s2)
    Let s4 = SnqbSeedSlice(s3)
    SnqbSeedSets(s4)
